From: MoveCertificate contributors
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: drop diagnostic queue trace from acquire replay fix

Patch 030 was developed on top of the opt-in queue tracing patches (028/029),
which the final performance-clean build excludes.  Remove the leftover
movecert_queue_trace() call so the functional acquire-replay fix no longer
references the diagnostic tracing helpers.

--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_queue.c
@@ -344,8 +344,7 @@
       sync = submit->_wait_temps[submit->wait_count] =
          semaphore->android_acquire_replay;
       semaphore->android_acquire_replay = NULL;
       semaphore->android_acquire_replay_queue = NULL;
-      movecert_queue_trace("acquire-replay", queue, submit, semaphore, sync, 0);
 #endif
    } else {
       if (semaphore->type == VK_SEMAPHORE_TYPE_BINARY) {
